            <ArticleTitle>Spontaneous double vessel coronary artery dissection. A case report and surgical management.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>181-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Spontaneous coronary artery dissection is an uncommon clinical entity, its presentation and management similar to atherosclerotic coronary artery disease. We report on a young adult male who presented with myocardial infarction due to simultaneous dissection of left anterior descending and right coronary artery. He was treated with bilateral interal mammary artery grafts.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
